From 972a7d9e238ea7f64ab60d9d589044acfe4a46f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:11:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fmradio: build out of tree on mainline 7.2 with our conninfra

Kbuild for the MT6635 / CONNAC2 configuration (mt6635_2_fm_lib,
plat/conn_infra). Mainline API: class_create(name), proc_ops, void
platform remove, timer_delete, ioremap, struct timeval replaced by a
same-layout fm_timeval (ioctl ABI kept).

Fixes: the module never freed its IRQ / register windows / conninfra
callbacks on unload (fm_wcn_ops_unregister was never called and
low_ops_unregister was not wired: a reload left the old handler on the
shared IRQ and the next FM interrupt reset the SoC); teardown now runs
every step. Suspend: a wakeup source while the receiver is powered and
-EBUSY from the PM prepare callback (suspending CONNSYS with FM on reset
the SoC); a player holds a logind sleep inhibitor, which the AOD honours.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013fD3if93WntovhmD8fGa8C
